WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.918
Processed food companies
spend a lot of effort

00:00:02.918 --> 00:00:06.060
trying to make their products seem
healthier than they actually are.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.918
Does vitamin and mineral fortification
make dayglow marshmallows healthy?

00:00:10.918 --> 00:00:12.734
Watch to find out.

00:00:12.963 --> 00:00:22.807
"Are Fortified Kids' Breakfast Cereals
Healthy or Just Candy?"

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.940
In 1941, the American Medical
Association's Council

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.800
on Foods and Nutrition was presented
with a new product, Vi-Chocolin,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.000
a vitamin fortified chocolate bar,
offered ostensibly as a product

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.800
of high nutritive value, but in reality,
intended for promotion to the public

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.260
as a kind of vitaminized candy.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.580
Surely something like that
couldn't happen today,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.200
but that's the entire sugary cereal
industry's business model.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.180
Twelve vitamins and minerals.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.220
Way better than those marshmallow
Froot Loops with just a measly 11.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.600
Nutrients are added to breakfast
cereals as a marketing gimmick

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.060
to create an aura of healthfulness.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.240
If those same nutrients
were added to soda,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.760
would we feed our kids
Coke for breakfast?

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.720
We might as well spray cotton
candy with vitamins too.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.060
As one medical journal
editorial read,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.260
Adding vitamins and minerals to
sugary cereals is worse than useless.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.760
The subtle message is that
somehow it's safe to eat more.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.320
General Mills' "Grow up strong with
Big G kids" cereals' ad campaign

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.040
featured products like Lucky
Charms, Trix, and Cocoa Puffs.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.700
That's like the dairy industry promoting
ice cream to get your calcium.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.180
Kids who eat presweetened
breakfast cereals may get

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.480
more than 20% of their daily
calories from added sugar.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.040
Most sugar in the American diet
comes from beverages like soda,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.640
but breakfast cereals represent the third
largest food source of added sugars

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.380
in the diets of children and adolescents,
wedged between candy and ice cream.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.680
On a per serving basis,
there is more added sugar

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.700
in a cereal like Frosted Flakes than
there is in frosted chocolate cake,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.560
brownies, or a frosted doughnut.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.540
Kellogg and General Mills argue that
breakfast cereals only contribute

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.420
a relatively small amount of
sugar to the diets of children,

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.040
less than soda, for example.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.000
This is a perfect example of
a psychological phenomenon

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.920
known as diffusion of responsibility.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.500
That's like every restaurant in the
country arguing that their individual

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.200
contribution to the problem of
second-hand smoke is relatively

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.400
tiny, therefore should be exempted
from the smoking ban.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.120
Each and every source of added
sugar should be reduced.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.760
The industry argues that most
of their cereals have less

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.440
than 10 grams of sugar per serving,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.400
but when Consumer Reports measured
how much youngsters actually poured,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.220
they were found to serve
themselves about 50% more

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.880
than the suggested serving size
for most of the tested cereals.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.580
The average portion of Frosted
Flakes they poured for themselves

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.440
contained 18 grams of sugarâ€”4.5
teaspoons, or 6 sugar packets worth.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.940
It's been estimated that a child
eating one serving a day

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.340
of the average children's
cereal would consume

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.680
close to 10 pounds of sugar in a year,
nearly 1,000 spoonfuls of sugar.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.840
General Mills offers the "Mary Poppins
defense," arguing that it's those

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.020
spoonfuls of sugar that help the
medicine go down, explaining that

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:27.420
if sugar is removed from bran cereal, it
would have the consistency of sawdust.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.680
If we couldn't add sugar, our
cereals would be unpalatable.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:39.240
If one has to add sugar to a product to
make it edible, that should be a sign.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.960
That's a characteristic of so-called
ultra-processed foods,

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.620
where you have to pack them full
of things like sugar, salt, flavorings

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.980
since they have had their natural
intrinsic flavors processed out,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:54.060
and you have to kind of mask any
unpleasantries in the final product.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.420
The president of the
Cereal Institute has argued

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.960
that without sugary cereals, kids
might not eat breakfast at all,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.080
similar to dairy industry arguments
that removing chocolate milk

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.500
from school cafeterias would
risk kids skipping lunch.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.340
He also stressed we must
consider the alternatives.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.640
As Kellogg's director
of nutrition once put it:

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.280
I would suggest that
Fruit Loops as a snack

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.400
are much better than potato
chips or a sweet roll.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.880
You know there's a problem when
the only way to make your product

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.540
look good is to compare it
to Pringles and Cinnabon.

